WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:06.320
On the king's orders, we are transporting 
these heretics to Radodorbo.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.980
<b>Traverse 5% of the map</b>

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.980
<b>Deliver the goods to Radodorbo</b>

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.980
<b>(Time limit: 40 days)</b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.820
Are these people the "goods"?

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.790
We are going to publicly execute 
them atop a hill there.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.060
But if we take them there, 
they're gonna be killed, including the kid.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.440
A human attack has been detec.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.290
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.290
<b>\h\h\hChef                              Rank 9→8</b>

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.150
Reducing your experi.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.810
<i>But it's okay if people die 
as a result of our actions?</i>

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.130
<i>Is this event part of the quest?</i>

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.860
<i>Or do we fail if we help them?</i>

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.620
<i>Which...</i>

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:38.370
<i>is it?!</i>

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.650
I don't believe the 
far western town of Radodorbo

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.400
falls under the Kingdom of Deokk's authority.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.360
You intend to execute your own 
citizens on foreign ground?

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.360
Who do you think you are? 
State your name!

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.880
I am Kahvel, a knight of the 
city-state of Cortonel.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.730
While your nation may be larger, 
you appear to be a mere foot soldier,

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.840
which means I am not obligated 
to submit to your questioning.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:34.820
Ah, Cortonel?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:38.420
The tiny nation with no value as anything 
but a significant traffic route?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.520
Well, pardon my rudeness.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.920
I am Vice Corporal Kamilto 
of the Kingdom of Deokk,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.860
and I am in command of this squad.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.930
A militant troop from a large nation 
with no talent for anything but war

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:53.770
had its highest officers killed by kobolds, 
and has the nerve to speak to me that way?

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.820
Wait just a minute!

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.750
The Kingdom of Deokk is a dictatorship that seeks
 to consolidate power over the entire continent!

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.880
We should carve up these three and 
bury them while we have the chance!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.780
I will not allow anyone to 
ridicule the Kingdom of Deokk!

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.590
Any who stand in our way will die!

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.440
U-Um...

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:19.500
Yotsuya-kun!

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.670
Oh, uh...

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.890
Heroes, gather!

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:29.360
This whole situation is an event we have to 
get through to deliver the goods to Radodorbo.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.260
And if it's a compulsory 
event, that means...

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.680
the "goods" we have to deliver must be...

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.750
Those people, right?

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.600
I get it now.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.950
So if we help those kingdom soldiers, 
we'll complete the quest, right?

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.960
Yes, but if we transport these prisoners,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.960
they'll all be executed, even this child.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.370
So that's the deal, huh?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.300
The people from the future may be 
watching to see if we'll sacrifice them.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.670
It's also possible the result of our actions 
will be considered a human attack,

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.230
which would mean game over for us.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.630
Wait, so it's a trap, then!

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.960
I'm just saying it's a possibility.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:09.930
In any case, I think it'd be pretty risky 
to kill those soldiers right now.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.200
So what do we do?

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.030
Oh, I just came up with an idea.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.440
Maybe we could see them 
as far as Radodorbo,

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.310
then stop the execution 
and set them all free?

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.110
Oh, that's possible.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.930
So, um...

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.480
Does everyone agree we should keep 
heading that way until we decide?

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.490
So that settles it.

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:33.900
I think that's the better option, too.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.880
Are you sure we should allow 
them to accompany us?

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.070
With a foreign knight among them, no less?

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.270
We have no choice.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:48.600
We can't kill the prisoners 
before their execution.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.790
We have no choice but to rely on 
the hero with the healing power.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.430
He still hasn't regained consciousness?

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.680
I think he's improving little by little,

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.480
but he <i>is</i> just a child.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.360
And I have to take breaks now and 
then since my MP is limited.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.020
<i>What we need is information. 
That comes first.</i>

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.080
We'll make camp here. 
You can agree to that, yes?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.160
Why must we take orders 
from a man like him?

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.240
Well, we're the ones who asked to 
be allowed to travel with them.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.800
<i>I don't know what it is...</i>

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:34.660
<i>but I just don't trust him.</i>

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:38.040
Excuse me, Kamilto-san.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.710
Don't hang around too long.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:44.840
Thanks.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.390
Thank you for inviting me.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:50.340
I thought you'd be worried 
about this child.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:52.670
I appreciate your consideration.

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.400
I am Fofcel, a missionary.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.790
I've come from the continent of Illa.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:00.120
I had hoped...

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:05.340
that Belili here could be spared, 
even if the rest of us cannot.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.290
<i>Huh...</i>

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.010
<i>There it is! So that's what 
the real goal is here?</i>

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:13.190
The Kingdom of Deokk 
kills all Arteros believers,

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.930
even those from other countries.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:18.830
He surely won't be afforded any 
protection in Radodorbo, either.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:24.020
If I may ask, what does this kingdom 
hate so much about Arteros?

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.410
The nation is divided between 
citizens who worship only the king

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:32.940
and citizens who worship 
both God and the king.

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:37.450
Both sides continue their hostilities, 
insisting that the other side started it,

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:39.720
leading to prolonged conflict in which

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:42.500
each side destroyed everything 
the other believed in.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.100
The destruction of the kingdom's successive 
leaders' statues was the final straw,

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:50.720
leading to the prohibition 
of the religion...

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.510
and the execution of its believers.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:55.840
For real?

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.240
Even for a dictatorship, 
executing people over statues is...

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.760
It is a complicated thing.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.130
In peaceful times, the god Jiusis 
advocates love and peace,

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:10.180
but some believers failed to comprehend what 
our scriptures said about love and peace,

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:14.020
and the people of the kingdom 
divided into "us" and "them."

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:18.460
<i>So the actions of a few radicals 
made everything worse.</i>

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.630
<i>Looks like this really 
is a compulsory event.</i>

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:26.550
I don't really get stuff like 
religion and dictatorships.

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:28.810
<i>So next is...</i>

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:30.490
<i>him.</i>

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.160
Kamilto-san.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.260
Why was it necessary to undergo

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:41.140
such a dangerous journey just to execute 
Arteros believers in Radodorbo?

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.440
To set an example, of course.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.000
They come here from the continent of Illa,

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.060
and since Radodorbo is the gateway to this 
continent, they must be halted there.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.770
It's vitally important 
to dampen their morale

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:57.320
as soon as they set foot here, 
to prevent them from propagating further.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.950
Is it really necessary 
to go to such lengths?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:02.670
Our king...

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.040
Father!

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.480
Father...

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:20.170
The fate of war orphans and families 
whose men could no longer work

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:21.460
was already set in stone.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:26.550
But it was the current king, 
Deokk V, who changed that history.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:30.580
I shall reward not only our soldiers 
who fought bravely in the war,

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:35.650
but also those who lost their fathers 
or sons, with one slave each!

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.880
The first step to the unification 
of this continent

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.460
is to improve the lives of the citizens!

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.940
To realize this goal, it is my intention

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:47.760
to continue establishing more 
colonies in the kingdom's name!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.350
My family was thus spared 
from homelessness.

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.300
Ours is a good king who 
never abandons the weak,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.300
and he truly desires a unified continent 
for the good of the people.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:04.480
To achieve that, the evil Arteros religion 
must be erased from this continent at any cost.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.620
Do you understand now?

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.410
Yes.

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.360
<i>Killing is definitely going too far,</i>

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.080
<i>but in these people's minds, 
that logic makes sense.</i>

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:23.490
<i>A guy who's colonizing smaller countries 
for slaves is "saving the weak"?</i>

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:26.610
<i>He's only saving the weak 
of his own nation.</i>

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.940
<i>That's just mob mentality.</i>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.480
How is that a good king?

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:32.580
What?

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:36.600
Yeah, I gave it some thought,

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:38.510
and I hate dictatorships.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.200
Uh, I'm still talking here—

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.180
I mean, don't you, too?

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:46.200
Like, bullies try to assert dominance 
based on certain social cues, right?

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.430
If someone makes waves and all 
the others turn on them,

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:51.870
they're demoted to a target, and the 
cycle of social cues goes on and on.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.990
But every now and then,

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:56.770
there's one who ignores the cues and goes 
crying to her boyfriend or a teacher.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.540
That's wrong, isn't it?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.270
We're not playing by those rules!

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:05.420
A big nation attacking smaller 
ones is just ganging up on them!

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:10.630
There's no humanity involved in a 
bunch of people ganging up on a few!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.160
You get what I mean?

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:15.590
<i>No humanity? What's she talking about?</i>

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:18.430
And once the few are made 
into slaves, they're done!

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:20.280
Where does he get off "rewarding" 
people with slaves?

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.010
Those aren't the king's slaves!

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:25.680
Okay, if nothing else, 
I get that you're pissed.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.250
I haven't understood a word you've said,

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.510
but I do understand that 
you're ridiculing my king!

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:32.430
Take it back or die!

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.620
Hey, Iu-san!

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:34.060
Eh?

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:37.240
There's no way we'll all die 
if we kill these guys!

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.100
Let's kill 'em!

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:42.680
She didn't say anything! I'm sorry! 
I'll give her a talking-to!

00:10:42.680 --> 00:10:45.310
And what is your opinion, then?

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:45.910
Huh?

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.890
Oh, uh, well... To each his own, I say!

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:53.330
And the king... isn't wrong 
as far as that logic goes.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:03.970
m 0 0 l 258 0 l 258 200 l 0 200

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:03.970
<b>[Horse]</b>

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:03.970
Equidae 
Hikoteri Horse

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:03.970
Unlike the creatures known as "horses" on Earth, they are omnivorous 
and walk on two legs. The standard cost of one horse is equivalent to
around 700,000 Japanese yen, but premium stock can sell for more 
than ten million. When not carrying any cargo, it can reach top speeds
of 70 to 120 kilometers per hour.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:17.560
You know, being women,

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.070
there's no way we'll ever 
match a man's strength.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:22.820
The question is how to 
make up that difference.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:23.960
With techniques...

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.750
Sword art, right?

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:31.430
Which means cutting locations that will 
cause instant death or a fatal wound.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.670
Do you know where those are?

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:34.740
Uh...

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.620
It will take seven days 
to cross this mountain.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:43.920
From there, it's five days to Radodorbo.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.060
<i>That's the first time he's spoken 
to me since two nights ago...</i>

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:53.300
So twelve more days until we get there...

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:57.110
And we have thirteen days and 
twenty hours left in our quest.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.370
It'll be close.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:00.860
Can we cross that mountain 
with horse-drawn carriages?

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:04.650
The steep slopes make it difficult, 
but not impossible.

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:07.580
However, there is an alternate route.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.240
It would be faster.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.980
This is killing me!

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.590
This is the second time I've 
pushed a carriage with you.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.810
Yeah, I guess so.

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:25.500
It won't be much longer. Let's keep it up!

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:26.260
Right!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.680
Hey, there it is! I see it!

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:38.100
What is that?

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.950
This is the alternate route?

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:52.720
The mechanisms throughout this cave 
were built thousands of years ago,

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:56.300
but we know that the one at the 
entrance is still functional.

00:12:56.570 --> 00:13:00.710
It does seem preferable to riding 
our carriages over the mountain...

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.780
Wait just inside for a bit.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:06.590
I'll activate the mechanism 
that'll allow us entry.

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.770
Got it.

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:14.030
Wow...

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:15.410
Incredible...

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:39.810
It's turning!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.780
That's so cool!

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.110
Whoa, wait!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.070
You're kidding me!

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.560
Open up!

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:51.780
Hey! Open up!

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:54.060
<i>We're... locked in?!</i>

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.070
I'm truly sorry about this,

00:13:57.070 --> 00:14:00.800
but we cannot travel with 
people who sympathize with

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.300
the followers of that evil religion!

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:03.300
You bastard!

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:06.730
I wish you great heroes all the best.

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:10.400
Though I can't say whether your 
strength will work against <i>that</i>...

00:14:11.090 --> 00:14:12.130
Come, let's go!

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.330
Great Hero!

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:14.270
Quiet!

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:17.560
Hey!

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.150
Damn him!

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:24.770
<i>We lost the prisoners that 
might be our "goods."</i>

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:27.010
<i>And time's running out.</i>

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.280
<i>I don't know if we can even get out.</i>

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.100
<i>Seriously? This is worse 
than where we started!</i>

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:47.280
This settles it. If we can get through 
here, it's a shortcut, right?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:51.470
So let's get through first, hack up those 
three, bury them, and be done with it.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:55.420
What do you say? Come on.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:58.730
Let's go!

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:16.590
Well, that's a pretty obvious trap!

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:39.320
<i>This pillar... should face this way.</i>

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.230
Hey, way to go!

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.240
Whoa, scary!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:30.330
This one should be easy!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:33.880
We're gonna get to the other side 
first and give that Deokk jerk a—

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:43.100
<b>Dead</b>

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:43.100
<b>Reviving in</b>

