00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:44.060
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:46.340
Damn it! I got careless!

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:49.150
Yotsuya-kun! What do you see down there?

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:52.290
Sorry! I can't climb back up!

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.300
Go on ahead if you can!

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.170
Seriously?

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.690
That's gotta be about an eight-story drop.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:04.460
<i>I don't think Yotsuya-kun will make 
it back to finish the fourth quest.</i>

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.370
Two of the walls move irregularly.

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:20.980
The ones further down seem to 
jump out at shorter intervals.

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:25.470
Since we have the carriages, 
we'd want at least 40 seconds.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:29.720
<i>We should've trusted Yotsuya-kun's 
plan for completing the quest.</i>

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:33.330
<i>If we'd just followed the plan, 
we'd be closer to our destination.</i>

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:35.280
<i>Can we finish the quest without him?</i>

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.910
<i>No, before that... can we get out of here?</i>

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:42.830
Fifteen...

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.050
What?

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:46.760
Um, hang on a minute.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:49.420
We have a pen and paper, right?

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:56.150
The food they dropped will 
hold me for half a day.

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:59.100
I need to find a way out 
before the sun goes down...

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:02.520
No, seriously, there's nothing 
but skeletons down here.

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:07.440
I'll try to count how long it takes for 
each wall to move again after it stops.

00:18:08.310 --> 00:18:11.350
I mean, it seems like there's 
some rule to it...

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:13.220
But what?

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.740
I think this trap is powered by water.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.200
Like those bamboo tubes that 
fill with water and drop?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.010
Based on the total number of seconds,

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:25.100
wouldn't that mean there are several 
of those things moving them?

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:28.980
There are two in front, 
one that moves every 60 seconds

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:30.690
and one that moves every 75 seconds.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:33.300
If that's right, their timing 
could be perfectly aligned.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:34.040
And the ones further back?

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.640
I've got it!

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:38.670
Yeah, this should do it.

00:18:38.670 --> 00:18:39.540
That means...

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:42.970
we should start moving at the end 
of the next 540-second cycle.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:45.460
Just to be safe, I'll go by myself.

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:45.880
What?

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:46.880
Iu-chan!

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:49.310
If it doesn't work, 
take care of the rest for me.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:02.780
She made it!

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:03.920
All right!

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:06.320
Yotsuya-kun, are you down there?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:08.370
Oh, yeah! I'm here!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.380
We're gonna go on ahead!

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.690
Got it! Thanks!

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:16.600
Okay... But, seriously, 
why are you being all polite?

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.260
Another dead end...

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:26.140
Seriously, though, what the 
heck was Yotsuya thinking?

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:29.360
W-Well, if not for him, we all 
would've been done for by now.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:32.340
You're right. So let's figure 
this out ourselves.

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:33.010
Yeah.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.820
<i>Figure something out...</i>

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.990
<i>I have to figure something out.</i>

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:50.070
It's cutting it! If I can 
make footholds with this...

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.220
What is this? An arena?

00:20:27.860 --> 00:20:30.610
And what's behind those doors?

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:54.530
A monster?!

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:55.640
Is that...

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.400
A gargoyle? I've never seen one before.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.550
A gargoyle?

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:01.570
A man-made creature.

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.200
Is it... dead?

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.890
I've heard that mummifying them 
by removing their body fluids

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:10.110
can allow them to move even 
after thousands of years...

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:15.510
Though I can't say whether your 
strength will work against <i>that</i>...

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:18.410
You don't think this is 
what he meant, do you?

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.770
I-It's starting to move...

